  "recent_hooks": [
    "The crypto market just erased $150 billion in value over 48 hours. When Bitcoin ($BTC) breaks below $69,000 while ETH ($ETH) drops toward $1,900, it is not a routine pullback; it is a rapid liquidation cascade. The question for traders now is whether this volume of accelerated selling pressure has found its bottom or if more downside is being priced in.",
    "+$16.9 billion flowed into Vanguard S&P 500 ETF ($VOO) across 5 trading days ending November 10th. In the same window, Invesco QQQ Trust ($QQQ) pulled in +$5.3 billion and Vanguard Total Stock Market ETF ($VTI) took +$3.3 billion. Capital isn't just sitting back during pullbacks\u2014it is actively hunting the dip.",
    "That is $250,000,000 wiped out in 10 minutes. Bitcoin dropped to $67,000 as a wave of leverage was forced out of the crypto market all at once. #bitcoin",
    "Democratic control of Congress and leadership turmoil at Nvidia ($NVDA) could push AI demand away from a single chip giant and toward rival semiconductor makers and rival Big Tech stocks, according to ETF experts.",
    "Tom Lee is blaming the recent crypto dump on a pileup of temporary pressure: Nvidia ($NVDA) margin calls, pre-Anthropic IPO selling, released hack funds, broader AI fear, and US chip-export scrutiny. His take is that the underlying SUPERCYCLE remains intact and these headwinds will pass.",
    "$230,000,000,000 left the crypto market cap in a single 24-hour drop.",
    "2.4% is the number to watch in Japan's prelim GDP deflator year-over-year. Markets expected 2.7%, down from the previous 2.6% reading, but the actual print missed both. Domestic inflation pressure isn't building quite as fast as the consensus laid out.",
    "Futures are pricing tech optimism ahead of Nvidia ($NVDA) earnings and the Anthropic IPO, with Nasdaq 100 futures up 0.7% while the S&P 500 gains 0.3% and the Dow Jones ticks up 0.2%. Market focus remains squarely on the major tech events setting the tone for the week.",
    "Leo KoGuan is freezing further investment, Elon Musk is offering to hire him, and 150k people have signed a petition to bring him back. The market is realizing that Nvidia Corporation ($NVDA) without Jensen Huang is a fundamentally different risk profile.",
    "251 BTC bought for $17.5M, averaging $69,853 per coin, bumps Strive\u2019s holdings to 43,404 BTC. The $10M raised through the $SATS ATM gives a liquidity cushion. Preferred dividend coverage now 133 months, a long runway. Amplification ratio at 76% $ASST $Strive, Inc. ($SATA) $SATS signals leveraged exposure.",
    "15 million records from Deutsche Bank ($DB) allegedly leak, exposing 3,000 transactions and roughly $582 million in suspicious payments linked to Jeffrey Epstein, alongside undisclosed financial dealings with Donald Trump and wealthy Russian clients.",
    "Anthropic ($ANT) just priced its IPO at $83 per share, blowing past its initial $70 to $78 marketed range.",
    "Take a look at sentiment right now. Because of a personal event involving Jensen Huang, there are now widespread calls that the \"AI bubble has popped.\" Sentiment is as though AI has failed, the inv...",
    "The S&P 500 ($SPX) has erased $6 trillion in value since its October 6th high after closing down for the 6th-straight day. With the Nasdaq 100 ($NDX) now down 15% from its own record high, the market is no longer just pulling back\u2014it is repricing tech leadership at a pace that wipes out months of gains in less than a week.",
    "The argument that tech stocks are cheap hinges entirely on believing the AI revolution is far from over. If Nvidia ($NVDA) handles its leadership transition and political headwinds soften, pulling back from this tech bear market might end up looking like the single best entry point of the decade."
  ],
